# MAGIC <div class="dbx">
# MAGIC <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">03</span><span class="sec-icon">⏰</span><h2>Triggers: when does a job run?</h2></div><div class="tbl"><table>
# MAGIC <thead>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <th>Trigger</th>
# MAGIC <th>Starts a run</th>
# MAGIC <th>Use when</th>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC </thead>
# MAGIC <tbody>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Manual / API</strong></td>
# MAGIC <td><em>Run now</em>, REST API, another orchestrator</td>
# MAGIC <td>Ad hoc runs, testing</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Scheduled</strong></td>
# MAGIC <td>Cron-style schedule with a time zone (UI or cron syntax)</td>
# MAGIC <td>Data arrives at <strong>known times</strong>; reports due at fixed times</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong>File arrival</strong></td>
# MAGIC <td>New files in a UC <strong>volume</strong> or <strong>external location</strong> (checked about every minute; use <strong>Test trigger</strong> to verify the path)</td>
# MAGIC <td>Files arrive at <strong>unpredictable</strong> times</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Table update</strong></td>
# MAGIC <td>One or more UC tables are updated</td>
# MAGIC <td>Run right after an upstream team's table changes</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC <tr>
# MAGIC <td><strong>Continuous</strong></td>
# MAGIC <td>A new run starts as soon as the previous one ends</td>
# MAGIC <td>Always-on streaming workloads</td>
# MAGIC </tr>
# MAGIC </tbody>
# MAGIC </table></div>
# MAGIC <p>Data-driven triggers (file arrival, table update) avoid <strong>empty runs</strong> and runs that start <strong>too early</strong>.</p>
# MAGIC </div>

