# MAGIC <div class="dbx">
# MAGIC <div class="sec-head"><span class="sec-num">06</span><span class="sec-icon">🩹</span><h2>When things fail</h2></div><ul>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Repair run:</strong> after a failure, re-run <strong>only the failed tasks and their dependents</strong>. Successful tasks are not executed again, which saves time and money.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Retries:</strong> per task, a retry count and interval. Retries are off by default for most tasks.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Timeout:</strong> the maximum duration of a task. When exceeded, the status is <em>Timed Out</em>. With retries, the timeout applies to each attempt.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Duration threshold:</strong> sends a <strong>warning</strong> only and does not stop the task.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> email, Slack or webhooks on start, success, failure or duration warning, at job or task level.</li>
# MAGIC <li><strong>Max concurrent runs:</strong> the default is <strong>1</strong>. Extra triggered runs are skipped unless <strong>queueing</strong> is enabled.</li>
# MAGIC <li>Task statuses to recognise: <em>Succeeded</em>, <em>Failed</em>, <strong><em>Upstream failed</em></strong> (a dependency failed), <em>Excluded</em> (condition not met), <em>Timed Out</em>, <em>Skipped</em>.</li>
# MAGIC </ul>
# MAGIC </div>

